{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfTgebZg5q1UTGUSZyAzN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create a summary of findings and move to the design phase:\n\n**Repository Findings:**\n- `ShipmentController` at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56`\n- `Shipment` model and `ShipmentStatus` enum at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`\n- `ShipmentRepository` (in-memory) at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`\n- Error handling via `ApiExceptions` at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:11-30`\n- `ErrorCode` enum at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler` at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29`\n- Tests at `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`\n\n**Conventions:**\n- POST endpoints for create operations return 201 status with `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...)`\n- GET operations return 200 with the resource or throw exceptions\n- `ConflictException` for 409 responses (e.g., duplicate resources)\n- `ResourceNotFoundException` for 404 responses\n- All errors use `ApiError` envelope with `error` field containing `code`, `message`, and `fields`\n- Error codes are feature-specific (ORDER_*, SHIPMENT_*)\n- Tests verify both status codes and error body structure using jsonPath assertions\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` - add confirm endpoint\n2. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` - add error code for invalid state\n3. `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking the idempotent requirement (confirm must succeed even if already confirmed)\n- Not handling all state transition cases (must handle CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- Inconsistent error responses with the rest of the API\n\n**Open questions:**\n- The ticket names all required cases clearly. No ambiguities.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed Change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add new error code:\n   - Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the `ErrorCode` enum to represent when a shipment is in a state that prevents the confirm operation\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add new endpoint:\n   - Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method\n   - Takes a shipment ID from the path\n   - Retrieves the shipment; throws `ResourceNotFoundException` with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` if not found (404)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, transitions to `CONFIRMED`, saves, and returns the updated shipment (200)\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, does nothing and returns the shipment unchanged (200 - idempotent)\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throws `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` (409)\n   - Returns 200 with the shipment in all success cases\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming a CONFIRMED shipment is idempotent (no change)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error envelope\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error envelope\n\n**Alternative Rejected:**\n- Could have used a generic exception for state errors, but this doesn't fit the existing pattern where every state problem has its own error code\n- Could have avoided adding error code by reusing VALIDATION_FAILED, but this is semantically wrong (it's not a validation error)\n- Could have made the confirm operation fail on CONFIRMED (non-idempotent), but the ticket explicitly requires idempotent behavior\n\n**Data and Error Flow:**\n\n**Case 1: Confirm CREATED shipment**\n- Read: Retrieve shipment by ID from repository\n- Check: status == CREATED\n- Write: Save updated shipment with status = CONFIRMED\n- Response: 200 OK with updated Shipment JSON\n\n**Case 2: Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment**\n- Read: Retrieve shipment by ID from repository\n- Check: status == CONFIRMED\n- Write: No write needed (idempotent)\n- Response: 200 OK with current Shipment JSON\n\n**Case 3: Confirm CANCELLED shipment**\n- Read: Retrieve shipment by ID from repository\n- Check: status == CANCELLED\n- Exception: Throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, message)`\n- Response: 409 Conflict with ApiError envelope\n\n**Case 4: Confirm non-existent shipment**\n- Read: Attempt to retrieve shipment by ID from repository\n- Result: null\n- Exception: Throw `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)`\n- Response: 404 Not Found with ApiError envelope\n\n**Test Strategy:**\n1. `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` - creates shipment, confirms it, verifies status changed to CONFIRMED\n2. `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment idempotently` - confirms twice, verifies returns 200 both times with same shipment\n3. `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` - directly saves a CANCELLED shipment, attempts confirm, expects 409 with error code\n4. `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` - attempts confirm on non-existent ID, expects 404 with error code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes according to the design:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":22428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":258},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":nu